# mdeai response style — easy, real-world, named tasks

**Pair with:** [`mdeai-workflow.mdc`](./mdeai-workflow.mdc) · [`mdeai-task-naming.mdc`](./mdeai-task-naming.mdc) · personas in `CLAUDE.md`

---

## 1. Lead with the answer

First sentence = **verdict or decision** (merge yes/no, blocker, score). For implementation work, include **change class D/C/U/S** ([`mdeai-workflow.mdc`](./mdeai-workflow.mdc)). Details after.

```text
✅ "Safe to merge PR #140 — test-only; do not close SAN-546 yet."
❌ "I reviewed the PR and looked at several aspects…" (bury the verdict)
```

**Shape:** (1) one-line answer → (2) short table or bullets → (3) detail only if needed → (4) next step.

---

## 2. Easy to understand

- Plain English; short sentences; define jargon once.
- Prefer a **table** over a wall of prose when comparing tasks, gates, or scores.
- No telegraphic shorthand (`SAN-546 partial harness flake J14` without names).
- Scores need **one line of meaning** (what the number blocks for whom).

---

## 3. Real-world framing (mdeai personas + surfaces)

Anchor explanations in **who on mdeai.co is affected**, not generic SaaS analogies. Translate infra/DB into **what someone sees or cannot do**.

| Persona | Use when explaining… |
|---------|----------------------|
| **Camila** | Rentals, chat, cards, pins, thread memory |
| **Andrés** | Paid ticket, wallet QR, `/me/tickets` |
| **Roberto** | Host wizard, publish, `/host/events`, `/host/event/new` |
| **Lucía** | Prod smoke, journey matrix, Playwright proof |
| **Patricia** | Admin, ledgers, booking queues, `ai_runs` observability |
| **Tourist** | Restaurants, cafés, nightlife, ADK grounding |
| **Sofía** | Floor, hooks, CI, migration review — say when impact is dev-only |

**Good vs bad:**

| ❌ Abstract | ✅ Real-world |
|------------|---------------|
| "31 rows have NULL `organizer_id`" | "Roberto opens `/host/events` and won't see 31 older catalogue events — they're discovery imports, not his publishes" |
| "SAN-492 not applied" | "Tourist can't book Mamacita for a private event yet — venue offerings tables don't exist on prod" |
| "Readiness 88" | "Schema is ready for a **branch PR**; Andrés still can't buy a ticket on prod until **SAN-178 · PAY-001** proof lands" |

**Example:** "Andrés still cannot complete a real purchase on mdeai.co — checkout code exists, but no prod proof in wallet" — not "the payment integration lacks E2E validation."

---

## 4. Always name tasks (never bare SAN-###)

**Enforced by:** [`mdeai-task-naming.mdc`](./mdeai-task-naming.mdc) (`alwaysApply: true`) — applies to **every chat reply**, including task lists, tables, blockers, and next steps.

Every mention of a Linear issue in **chat** uses the full form:

```text
SAN-### · SPEC-ID — <Linear title>
```

**First mention in a reply** — markdown link with full link text:

```markdown
[SAN-178 · PAY-001 — Live ticket purchase on production](https://linear.app/sanjiovani/issue/SAN-178/pay-001-live-ticket-purchase-on-production)
```

| OK in chat | Not OK |
|------------|--------|
| "Blocker: **SAN-178 · PAY-001** — Andrés paid ticket" | "SAN-178 is open" |
| "Merge helps **SAN-546 · OPS-JOURNEY** J14/J15 harness" | "fixes 546" |
| Table column `Task (full name)` | Table column `SAN` only |

**Exceptions (narrow):** git branch `ai/san-546-…` · PR footer `Closes SAN-546` · filename `SAN-546-j14-j15-prod.spec.ts` — still spell out full name in the same paragraph once.

**Unsure of title?** `get_issue` via Linear MCP before writing.

**No classic SPEC-ID?** Use the Linear title prefix — e.g. `SAN-858 · DATA-QUALITY — Events Ownership Classification` (not `SAN-858`).

**Events board examples (copy pattern):**

```markdown
[SAN-178 · PAY-001 — Live ticket purchase on production](https://linear.app/sanjiovani/issue/SAN-178)
[SAN-492 · EVT-033 — Event venue + offerings schema](https://linear.app/sanjiovani/issue/SAN-492)
[SAN-858 · DATA-QUALITY — Events ownership classification](https://linear.app/sanjiovani/issue/SAN-858)
```

---

## 5. Audits, PR reviews, and checklists

Use this header pattern:

```markdown
**Verdict:** <one line>

| Check | Result |
|-------|--------|
| [SAN-828 · UX-043 — …](url) | 🟢 Done |
```

- Separate **merge safety** vs **production sign-off** vs **MVP exit** — do not collapse into one optimistic %.
- Call out **false positives** (e.g. weak test assertion that passed but stricter test fails on prod).

---

## 6. Anti-patterns

- ❌ Generic "imagine a user…" / Stripe-as-default analogies
- ❌ `89% launch ready` without saying **which gate** (concierge vs Andrés G1)
- ❌ Listing five SAN IDs with no SPEC-ID or persona
- ❌ Engagement bait ("Let me know if you want me to…") — end with one clear next step if needed

---

## Quick checklist (every non-trivial reply)

- [ ] First sentence = answer
- [ ] Task IDs include **SPEC-ID + title** (linked on first use)
- [ ] Impact named for a **persona + surface** (`/chat`, `/me/tickets`, …)
- [ ] Tables used for gates/scores/comparisons
- [ ] Next step is concrete (command, PR action, or blocker owner)
